Output post-processing for the OpenGL renderer, and a pause-menu A/B toggle.

A chain that runs on the finished picture at output resolution - after the
present/downsample filter, before the host OSD, rewind strip and menus, which
stay untouched on top:

  anti-aliasing   FXAA (classic reduction) or SMAA 1x (GLSL rendering of the
                  reference SMAA.hlsl, HIGH preset without diagonal search;
                  the reference AreaTex/SearchTex embedded in gpu_smaa_tex.h,
                  area zlib-compressed, MIT notice kept)
  sharpening      contrast-adaptive, after AMD FidelityFX CAS (MIT)
  bloom           soft-knee threshold on (colour^2), 5-level dual-filter
                  down/up chain in RGBA16F, normalised by level count
  grade           brightness, contrast, saturation, gamma, temperature
  vignette, film grain, and an 8-bit output dither whenever grade or bloom
  moved a value

Settings come from PSX_POSTFX (gpu_postfx.c), semicolon key=value pairs in the
launcher's percent units; unknown keys are ignored and values clamped. Nothing
set means nothing runs: gpu_gl_renderer.c draws exactly as before.

Hook: the three draws of the game image into the window - present_target_quad
(VRAM, native-wide and hold-last presents), interp_draw_quad (frame blending)
and the CPU/FMV present - go through image_target_begin/_end. With the chain
active the image is drawn into an lw x lh target TOP ROW FIRST (the present
UV rect is flipped for it), every pass works in that D3D-style orientation -
what SMAA's lookup tables and offsets assume, and what a D3D12 backend can
reuse unchanged - and the composite flips back into the letterbox viewport.
A hold-last redraw of the captured drawable is already post-processed and
bypasses the chain. glpfx_shutdown runs before the context is destroyed.

Texture dedither (dedither=1): TEX_FS softens the checkerboard dither painted
into texture art. With nearest sampling, a texel within 2.5/31 of its four
neighbours' mean, whose opposite neighbours agree, is pulled halfway to that
mean; larger differences (edges, lines, text) and cutout borders are kept.
Four extra texel fetches, only when enabled.

Pause menu: a POST FX row (ON / OFF, NONE when the launcher set nothing)
switches the chain and the dedither for the session. The menu now has twelve
rows, so rows are 26 px on a 28 px pitch from y=56 to keep clear of the footer.

Checked offline on the target driver (NVIDIA 617.14, RTX 5070): all nine
chain programs and the modified TEX_FS compile and link, and the chain run
on a test image gives the expected FXAA/SMAA edge smoothing in the right
orientation, neutral output identical to input, and bloom/grade/vignette/
grain as intended.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

