+## SMAA — Enhanced Subpixel Morphological Antialiasing
+
+[SMAA](https://github.com/iryoku/smaa) by Jorge Jimenez, Jose I. Echevarria,
+Belen Masia, Fernando Navarro and Diego Gutierrez, licensed **MIT** (the notice
+is reproduced in `runtime/src/gpu_smaa_tex.h`). The post-processing chain's
+SMAA 1x passes in `runtime/src/gpu_gl_postfx.c` are a GLSL rendering of the
+reference `SMAA.hlsl`, and `runtime/src/gpu_smaa_tex.h` embeds the reference
+AreaTex and SearchTex lookup textures (generated data, the area table
+zlib-compressed). The license states that the notice need not ship with binary
+distributions; it is kept in the source regardless.
+
+## AMD FidelityFX CAS — Contrast Adaptive Sharpening
+
+The sharpening pass in `runtime/src/gpu_gl_postfx.c` follows AMD's
+[FidelityFX CAS](https://github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-CAS) (no
+scaling, 3x3 soft min/max shaping), which AMD publishes under the **MIT**
+license. It is a re-implementation of the published algorithm in GLSL; no AMD
+source file is vendored.
